menu "Bin Light Configuration"

    config BINLIGHT_WIFI_SSID
        string "Wi-Fi SSID (optional, development only)"
        default ""
        help
            Optional since AutoAP provisioning landed (SPEC.md 3.4). Leave
            empty for normal builds: the device will raise its own setup
            network and be provisioned from a browser, and those credentials
            are stored in NVS. A value here is only a convenience for the
            developer's own bench device, and is used solely when nothing has
            been provisioned yet. Deliberately empty in the repo so no real
            credential is ever committed - your value lives in sdkconfig,
            which is gitignored.

    config BINLIGHT_WIFI_PASSWORD
        string "Wi-Fi Password (optional, development only)"
        default ""
        help
            See BINLIGHT_WIFI_SSID. Optional; provisioned credentials in NVS
            always take priority over anything compiled in.

    config BINLIGHT_WIFI_MAXIMUM_RETRY
        int "Wi-Fi connect attempts at boot before falling back to AutoAP setup mode"
        default 10

    config BINLIGHT_SNTP_SERVER
        string "SNTP server hostname"
        default "pool.ntp.org"

    config BINLIGHT_TZ_STRING
        string "POSIX TZ string"
        default "AEST-10AEDT,M10.1.0/2,M4.1.0/3"
        help
            Melbourne, Australia: AEDT starts first Sunday of October,
            ends first Sunday of April.

    config BINLIGHT_LED_GPIO
        int "WS2812 data GPIO"
        default 0

    config BINLIGHT_RESET_BUTTON_GPIO
        int "Reset button GPIO (-1 to disable)"
        default 9
        help
            Hold 3s to restart, 10s to factory reset (SPEC.md 3.12). The LEDs
            show which action is armed while you hold, so it needs no timing
            by feel.

            Defaults to 9, which on the Seeed XIAO ESP32-C6 is the existing
            BOOT button - no extra hardware needed. Note GPIO9 is a strapping
            pin: holding it down *while the device powers up* puts the chip
            into serial download mode instead. That only affects power-on, not
            presses during normal running, and is also how you'd deliberately
            enter flashing mode. Set to -1 to disable the button entirely, or
            change it if you wire a dedicated button to another pin.

    config BINLIGHT_RESET_BUTTON_ACTIVE_LOW
        bool "Reset button reads low when pressed"
        default y
        help
            True for a button wired to ground with a pull-up, which is how the
            XIAO's BOOT button (and most such buttons) work.

endmenu
